      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Based on the benchmarks done by Jelle there is still a pretty substantial performance benefit to having native VRCConstraints on your avatar vs ones auto-converted at runtime (https://vrc.school/docs/Other/Benchmarks/#59ace515859342c0b58324f69473f172). \n\nI agree that the auto fix button should never break a users project. But I do think that it would be a good idea to prod the user towards doing the conversion. Just maybe with some sort of forced/heavily encouraged backup, and a warning.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
