        "like": 2
      },
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": "66bf225e567f83c8082076ac",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "tracked",
      "value": "As mentioned earlier, there are performance benefits to uploading your avatar with VRChat constraints instead of Unity constraints. This is because as part of the auto-conversion process on avatars still using Unity constraints, we need to remap any animations affecting those Unity constraints onto the VRChat constraints replacing them. Since it isn't possible to redirect animations at runtime in Unity, we need to keep the Unity constraints disabled and copy animated changes to them over to the associated VRChat constraints just before they run each frame. This process has an overhead cost that scales with how many Unity constraints there are. This cost can be avoided entirely by using and animating VRChat constraints directly, which is why the SDK recommends converting to them before uploading.\n\nThe auto-fix option is known to be working as intended for avatar projects that do not include any custom user tooling like Modular Avatar or VRCFury. For those that do, we are currently working through adding the necessary support to let these tools properly integrate with the converter. This has been tracked here: https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/sdk-370-beta1-please-provide-a-hook-for-supplying-additional-animation-clips-and\n\nWe hope that these changes will allow user tools like this to function correctly once their authors have integrated them with VRChat's SDK.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
