      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "> 2. Even when we adapt to that API, when you have multiple avatars in your project, the auto fix will break any avatars other than the one that is selected, if they share the same animation clip assets.\n\n> 3. If your constraint-using system is a prefab, then the autofix will leave the prefab broken.\n\nAs a workaround for 2 and 3, I made Unity to VRC Constraint converter which applies to whole project preserving constraint data and prefab overrides. https://github.com/anatawa12/ProjectWideVRCConstraintsConverter",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
