  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-08-15T02:04:11.377Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Autoconversion of constraints on one avatar can cause breakage in a number of ways:\n\n1. Until MA and Fury adapt to the as-yet-unavailable API in https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/sdk-370-beta1-please-provide-a-hook-for-supplying-additional-animation-clips-and - this auto fix will break constraint-using gimmicks that are merged using these systems.\n\n2. Even when we adapt to that API, when you have multiple avatars in your project, the auto fix will break any avatars other than the one that is selected, if they share the same animation clip assets.\n\n3. If your constraint-using system is a prefab, then the autofix will leave the prefab broken.\n\nThese are a bit of a landmine for casual users. And, in most cases, this isn't necessary - VRChat will convert these at runtime, so the conversion is only helpful for a gimmick creator who is trying to debug differences between VRCConstraint and unity constraints.\n\nProviding an auto fix that can break users' projects is a sure way to lose trust in \"auto fix\" buttons in general; since there isn't much gain from most users pushing this button, I would suggest removing the auto fix prompt, making it just a warning, and providing a manual option to convert these constraints, with a corresponding help page describing some of the pitfalls.",
